<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beni Hasan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beni Hasan is an ancient cemetery on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-egypt">Middle Egypt</a>, near Minya. Its rock-cut tombs of the Eleventh and Twelfth Dynasties belonged to the nomarchs of the Oryx <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nome">nome</a>, and their paintings show daily life, wrestling, warfare and a caravan of Asiatic traders in the tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khnumhotep-ii">Khnumhotep II</a>. They are a major source for provincial society in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beni-hasan.jpg" alt="Beni Hasan" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Markh at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Exterior_view_of_tombs_of_Khety_and_Barquet_III.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
